PMB OS patch: glibc system paths relative to $PMBOS_ROOTFS (no chroot/proot needed)
Upstream: glibc 2.36 as shipped by Debian bookworm (source package glibc 2.36-9+deb12uN,
          checked against 2.36-9+deb12u14, i.e. after Debian's own quilt series)
          https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/g/glibc/glibc_2.36-9+deb12u14.dsc
          (also applies to the plain https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/glibc/glibc-2.36.tar.xz)
Apply:    patch -p1 --fuzz=0 < glibc-2.36-pmbos-rootfs.patch   (stages/stage-glibc.sh)

Why: PMB OS runs this glibc from an unpacked tree (imagefs) inside the Android app's data
directory. Android has no /etc/resolv.conf, /etc/hosts, /etc/nsswitch.conf, /etc/services,
/etc/protocols, /etc/passwd, /etc/group, /etc/localtime and no /bin/sh, and libc opens these
itself by absolute path - internal calls that LD_PRELOAD cannot interpose. Result without the
patch: DNS fails (getaddrinfo/res_init), user/service lookups fail, system()/popen() fail.

What: one internal header, include/pmbos-rootfs.h, with __pmbos_rootfs_path (PATH, BUF,
SIZE): when PMBOS_ROOTFS is set (secure_getenv semantics: ignored for AT_SECURE) to an
absolute path other than "/", returns "$PMBOS_ROOTFS" + PATH in BUF (PATH_MAX bytes on the
caller's stack); otherwise - or if the result would not fit - returns PATH unchanged. There is
no "exists?" fallback while the variable is set (deterministic, no TOCTOU between change
detection and open, the host's /system/etc/hosts is never mixed in). Unset -> byte-for-byte
upstream behaviour. Call sites (all in libc.so.6; nss_files/nss_dns are built into libc since
2.34, so libnss_files.so.2/libresolv.so.2 need no change):

  nss/nss_files_fopen.c    __nss_files_fopen: every nss_files database - /etc/passwd, group,
                           shadow, gshadow, hosts, services, protocols, networks, ethers, rpc,
                           netgroup, aliases (+ initgroups, nss_compat)
  nss/nss_database.c       nss_database_reload (fopen) and nss_database_check_reload_and_get
                           (change detection) of _PATH_NSSWITCH_CONF (/etc/nsswitch.conf)
  resolv/res_init.c        __resolv_conf_load: fopen (_PATH_RESCONF) (/etc/resolv.conf)
  resolv/resolv_conf.c     __resolv_conf_get_current: change detection of _PATH_RESCONF
  resolv/res_hconf.c       do_init: default _PATH_HOSTCONF (/etc/host.conf; RESOLV_HOST_CONF
                           still overrides it)
  sysdeps/posix/getaddrinfo.c  gaiconf_init (fopen) / gaiconf_reload (stat) of /etc/gai.conf
  time/tzfile.c            __tzfile_read: TZDEFAULT (/etc/localtime, TZ unset or equal to it)
                           and the default TZDIR (/usr/share/zoneinfo) for relative TZ names
                           (an explicit $TZDIR still wins)
  sysdeps/posix/system.c   do_system: posix_spawn path of SHELL_PATH (/bin/sh), argv[0] "sh"
  libio/iopopen.c          spawn_process: popen's _PATH_BSHELL
  posix/wordexp.c          exec_comm_child: command substitution shell (argv[0] + spawn path)
  posix/execvpe.c          maybe_script_execute: execvp/execvpe ENOEXEC fallback to /bin/sh

Not patched (on purpose): sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/spawni.c maybe_script_execute only exists
for GLIBC_2.2..2.15 compat symbols (SHLIB_COMPAT is false on aarch64, the oldest ABI is
GLIBC_2.17); getusershell (/etc/shells); ld.so (/etc/ld.so.cache, /etc/ld.so.preload - the
launcher sets LD_LIBRARY_PATH); gconv/locale dirs (GCONV_PATH, LANG=C.UTF-8 in the env
contract); nscd. The PMB OS launcher exports PMBOS_ROOTFS=<abs imagefs, no trailing slash>
to every process (pmbos/docs/subsystems/packbuilder.md, "Required environment").

--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/pmbos-rootfs.h
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+/* PMB OS: relocate glibc's fixed system paths into $PMBOS_ROOTFS.
+
+   PMB OS runs this glibc from an unpacked directory tree ("imagefs") inside
+   an Android app's data directory, without chroot/proot.  Android has no
+   /etc/resolv.conf, /etc/hosts, /etc/nsswitch.conf, /etc/passwd, ... and no
+   /bin/sh, and libc opens these by absolute path internally (not
+   interposable with LD_PRELOAD).  The launcher exports
+   PMBOS_ROOTFS=<absolute imagefs path> to every process; the few libc call
+   sites that open such a path pass it through __pmbos_rootfs_path first.
+
+   Semantics: if PMBOS_ROOTFS is set (ignored in AT_SECURE processes, like
+   every secure_getenv variable), starts with '/', is not "/" and
+   "$PMBOS_ROOTFS" + PATH (trailing slashes of the variable stripped) fits
+   into BUF, the joined path is returned in BUF; otherwise PATH itself is
+   returned unchanged.  There is no existence fallback: with PMBOS_ROOTFS
+   set, only the rootfs copy is consulted.  With the variable unset this
+   glibc behaves exactly like the unpatched one.  No allocation, no locks
+   (getenv, strlen and memcpy only).  */
+
+#ifndef _PMBOS_ROOTFS_H
+#define _PMBOS_ROOTFS_H 1
+
+#include <limits.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+/* Size of the caller-provided buffers.  */
+#define PMBOS_ROOTFS_BUFSIZE PATH_MAX
+
+static inline const char *
+__pmbos_rootfs_path (const char *path, char *buf, size_t size)
+{
+  const char *root = __libc_secure_getenv ("PMBOS_ROOTFS");
+  if (root == NULL || root[0] != '/' || path == NULL || path[0] != '/')
+    return path;
+  size_t rlen = strlen (root);
+  while (rlen > 0 && root[rlen - 1] == '/')
+    --rlen;
+  if (rlen == 0)
+    return path;
+  size_t plen = strlen (path) + 1;
+  if (rlen + plen > size)
+    return path;
+  memcpy (buf, root, rlen);
+  memcpy (buf + rlen, path, plen);
+  return buf;
+}
+
+#endif /* pmbos-rootfs.h */
